KG42.register("clusters-10ee9e0a3ecab305d8f4c5e7",{"id":"15-multiagent_reverse_auction::v142-d-K003","paper":"15-multiagent_reverse_auction","label":"Allocation and execution of qualified supply and conditional utility-grid supplementary purchase","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K003","label":"Allocation and execution of qualified supply and conditional utility-grid supplementary purchase","market_meaning":"Given hourly demand, submitted bids, and qualified suppliers, the aggregator arranges local supply and sends power references to qualified bidding agents for implementation by the executor. The residual external purchase branch when there is participation but supply is insufficient, and the full external purchase branch when all floor prices are higher and no one participates, are retained; the specific allocated quantities and eligibility order are still not closed.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","clearing","coordination","activation","matching"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The scope is limited to hourly procurement and execution of the grid-connected microgrid. The shared demand and bid chains provide inputs; R008 provides an interface only through the possibility of multiple suppliers, and its single-remaining-supplier description is not regarded as a resolved eligibility algorithm. Full external purchase with no participation and supplementary purchase after partial DER procurement apply separately and are not automatically extended to islanding or real-time loss-balancing rules.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Demand and qualified supply determine allocation; allocation produces execution power references; insufficient procurement separately triggers utility-grid supplementary purchase, forming a candidate rule from procurement responsibility to power-supply execution. Insufficient closure of eligibility ordering and allocation keeps it partial; shared inputs do not add to the number of independent rules.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Carries the qualified-supply check, the allocation to the first and subsequent suppliers, and the procurement arrangement under insufficient supply."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Supplements the execution responsibility for the allocation result and retains the two types of utility-grid external-purchase conditions and their outcomes."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Cites the estimated demand for the next hour as the information input for the allocation check; primary ownership remains with the bid-interaction cluster."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"shared","role":"support","rationale":"Cites the bids received by the aggregator and the verbal procurement objective; bid receipt is not equivalent to eligibility determination and does not prove lowest-cost optimality."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Only borrows the multi-supplier permission and allocation section of C001 for comparison; the termination ambiguity of C002 is retained, and it cannot be asserted on this basis that an ordered set of qualified suppliers has been obtained."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E19"],"rationale":"The estimated procurement demand for the same hour becomes the object of the qualified-supply coverage check and the residual-demand allocation; the two chains have no typed demand variable that could be merged separately."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E19"],"rationale":"The available-power bids received by the aggregator provide information for the subsequent check of qualified suppliers' coverage capability, and the two chains also retain a common verbal procurement objective; eligibility is not inferred from bid receipt, and the power and energy wording is not rewritten into the same optimization formula."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E19"],"rationale":"When a single seller cannot meet demand, multiple qualified sellers are permitted, which is complementary to the allocation scope in which other suppliers bear the residual demand after the first supplier is insufficient; the permission itself does not define the ordering of the first and second suppliers."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g01-E20"],"rationale":"The allocation section determines the use of the power references, and the execution section specifies that these references are communicated to qualified bidding agents and the executor and implemented. This connects the allocation output with execution responsibility and does not create a separate temporal or quantitative scientific edge."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E21"],"rationale":"The branch with participation and insufficient total supply appears in the allocation chain as a procurement arrangement and in the execution chain as DER procurement plus utility-grid supplementary purchase; only this branch is combined and it is not conflated with full external purchase when there is no participation."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-M01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R007::V::clearing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::V::clearing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g01-E20"],"rationale":"Both references carry the local allocation function for the same hour, and the execution chain cites its result; only the display of the function node is unified."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-M02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R004::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R007::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E21"],"rationale":"The demand announcement, bid collection, procurement arrangement, and communication of power references are all the responsibility of the aggregator in this mechanism; citing the same subject does not mean that all its behaviors belong to the same scientific constraint."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-M03","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R005::V::bidding.supply"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R005::V::bidding.supply","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E19"],"rationale":"Both cite the same supply-submission function, used respectively for collecting bids and checking qualified bids; all submitters are not equated with the set of qualified suppliers."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-M04","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R007::V::matching.counterparties","v141-c-R008::V::matching.counterparties"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E17"],"rationale":"Both are references to the qualified-supplier matching function, but enforcing eligibility conditions and the eligibility-generation process have different uses; unresolved issues concerning the number and ordering of suppliers cannot disappear through merged display."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-M05","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C006"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C006","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E21"],"rationale":"The two complete procedural statements have the same trigger condition, aggregator responsibility, and outcome of DER procurement plus residual utility-grid purchase, differing only in functional perspective. The complete supplementary-purchase statement is selected as the display representative, and all original constraints are retained; R007-C003 is only part of these activities and is not folded in together."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G01","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Demand, qualified submitted quantity, qualified amount, majority, and each supplier's power reference lack clear quantity definitions and allocation expressions; lowest cost is currently only a verbal objective, and the feasibility or optimality of the allocation cannot be tested.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E21"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"According to the existing R004 revision request, check back with the source for quantities, units, domains, and allocation definitions; when the source has no mathematical definition, continue to retain the procedural branch, and D does not invent an allocation formula or a lowest-cost optimization model."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G02","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R008 does not define the ordering of the first and second qualified suppliers, and its single-remaining-supplier statement cannot directly provide the second supplier required for the residual allocation in R004. The eligibility input required by the execution chain has not yet been provided by a complete, conflict-free selection rule.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C004","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g02-e021"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check together with the conflicts in the eligibility and pricing clusters, and clarify the qualified set, ordering, and conditions for multiple suppliers to enter; before resolution, treat eligibility as a conditional input and do not use the allocation narrative to retroactively fabricate a selection algorithm."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G03","category":"ontology_extension","description":"Full or residual supply from the utility grid is still carried by the existing clearing and execution functions, and the proposal for a dedicated supplementary-purchase node has not been approved. The statement that real-time losses and imbalance are made up by the utility grid has different trigger conditions and cannot be incorporated into this cluster's market-supply-insufficiency branch.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C005","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E23"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-P02"],"required_work":"Manually check whether the supplementary-purchase function requires ontology extension, and distinguish the auction procurement gap from real-time physical imbalance; for now retain the frozen constraints and do not add new nodes, frequency equations, or loss obligations."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G04","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The non-participation branch of Algorithm 1 includes the case in which the DER floor price equals the utility-grid floor price, whereas the full external purchase source also describes the case in which all floor prices are higher and no one is willing to participate. The full external purchase branch cannot be unconditionally generalized to all no-participation cases.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g02-e002"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check whether full external purchase takes no participation as a sufficient condition, and how equal floor prices or other exit reasons are handled; when the source is unclear, retain the existing complete condition and do not expand the exception branch."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G05","category":"unverified_source","description":"The B evidence for allocation, execution, and utility-grid supplementary purchase is all unverified, and the current C2 bindings and revision requests do not mean that an independent scientific review has been completed in this round.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E21"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check each chain and assembly mapping, especially verifying allocation responsibility, eligibility prerequisites, and supplementary-purchase conditions; keep all original objects and current source status unchanged."}]},"rule_refs":["15-multiagent_reverse_auction::v141-c-R004","15-multiagent_reverse_auction::v141-c-R007","15-multiagent_reverse_auction::v141-c-R002","15-multiagent_reverse_auction::v141-c-R005","15-multiagent_reverse_auction::v141-c-R008"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-143910e2088c2223","COMP-334f35169e6933ed","COMP-443a9bf9853dcd78","COMP-8ae9e2dee736e7c9","COMP-b646a091517c6af0","COMP-efa6e37c97477e8a"]});
